      "facts": [
        "Two questions, each a fixed option list (the referral one with a free-text \"Other\"). Shared between the form, the persistence layer and the admin view so a renamed option cannot silently split one answer into two in the analytics.",
        "Set only on `RETIRED_ONBOARDING_QUESTIONS`: the UTC day the form stopped asking it. Same meaning as `OnboardingRetiredOption.retiredOn`.",
        "No write-in since 2026-11-21: Operations and Creative were added to cover what it mostly held, and the six options are meant to be exhaustive. Answers from before stay counted here.",
        "Questions the form asked once and no longer does. Not offered, not accepted by validation, and not needed for an account to count as complete, but still tallied and shown in the admin view so their answers stay readable.",
        "Every question with answers on record, asked or retired: what the admin view and every tally count. The form, validation and the completeness check use `FREEBUFF_ONBOARDING_QUESTIONS` alone.",
        "The onboarding questions, one step each (2026-11-22): asked inside the welcome instead of in a card over the chat after the first send."
