        "title": "Add host platform override to SDK run options",
        "summary": "The SDK now supports a `hostPlatform` option that overrides the reported operating system for a run. This allows hosted runners to report the user's local environment (e.g., `win32` on a Linux server) so the model generates commands compatible with the user's shell and filesystem. The new `applyHostPlatform` function is called during `runOnce` and updates the session's `systemInfo.platform`, while leaving the `shell` configuration unaffected.",
